# Third-party notices

## MSA Sans (src/ui/fonts/)

The UI typeface is a subset of **Gowun Dodum** (고운돋움) by Yanghee Ryu (류양희),
licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The full licence text is in
`src/ui/fonts/OFL.txt`, and the copyright and licence records are preserved
inside the font binary itself.

- Upstream: https://github.com/yangheeryu/Gowun-Dodum
- Distributed via: https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/gowundodum
- Version subsetted: 2.000
- Presented as "MSA Sans". Gowun Dodum declares **no** Reserved Font Name, so
  OFL 1.1 §3 does not require the rename; it is a project convention, so that a
  packaged build and a machine with the font already installed resolve to the
  same metrics under the same family name. The copyright (name ID 0), licence
  (13) and licence URL (14) records are carried through unchanged, and the
  unique-ID record names what this file actually is.

## MSA Display (src/ui/fonts/)

The display typeface is a subset of **NanumMyeongjo ExtraBold** (나눔명조) by NHN
Corporation, designed by FONTRIX, licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
The full licence text is in `src/ui/fonts/OFL-NanumMyeongjo.txt`.

- Upstream: https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/nanummyeongjo
- Version subsetted: 2.032

**The rename is required, not a convention.** Nanum declares Reserved Font Names
— "Nanum", "NanumMyeongjo" and others — and OFL 1.1 §3 forbids a Modified
Version from using them. A subset is a Modified Version, so this file may not be
called Nanum anything. It is presented as "MSA Display". The copyright (name ID
0) is carried through unchanged and the licence records (13, 14) say what this
file is and where the licence lives.

### Why a second face at all

`MSA Sans` is a text face with no ambition to be a headline, and that was the
right half of §5's brief. The other half — the expressive display voice — was
being drawn as vector strokes (`src/ui/lettering.js`). Strokes of a constant
width make a geometric letter; the references this direction is built on are
high-contrast **serif** Korean, and stroke contrast is not something a stroke
renderer can fake. So the display half became a face.

`lettering.js` did not go away and must not: it composes any Hangul syllable from
jamo, so anywhere user input can reach — nicknames — still belongs to it. This
face is for **authored strings only**, which is what lets the subset be tiny.

### What was kept

| range | why |
|---|---|
| `한 여 름 알 까 기` | The game's name, set as the home screen's display type. |
| `0-9` | The date stamp, and any large numeral set in the display voice. |

**That is the whole subset — 17 glyphs, 3 KB.** It is safe because nothing user-
supplied is ever set in this face. **If you set a new authored string in
`MSA Display`, add its syllables here and re-subset**, or it renders as tofu with
no error. The subset command is in this file's history; `pyftsubset --text=...`
with `--name-IDs` is the whole of it.

### Weight

One static face, declared `font-weight: 400`. The source is ExtraBold, but it is
the only weight in this family, so declaring it 400 is what stops a browser
synthesising a bolder one on top of an already-heavy face. Same reasoning as
`FONT_WEIGHTS` for the text face, below.

